    "title": "Uninstalling USBLAN Drivers & Driver Store Cleanup",
    "url": "/uninstalling.html",
    "date": null,
    "text": "Uninstalling\nUse this procedure to remove USBLAN driver instances and related driver packages on Windows 11 lab and support systems.\nScope\nWindows 11 amd64\nWindows 11 arm64\nSingle or multiple attached USB networking devices\nStandard removal sequence\nDisconnect the target device when possible to avoid immediate re-enumeration.\nRemove the installed device instance from Device Manager (or equivalent scripted workflow).\nEnumerate matching driver packages in the driver store.\nDelete the target package from the driver store when complete uninstall is required.\nReconnect device only after confirming expected package/version state.\nCommand-line workflow (example)\nFor scripted support, use pnputil to inspect and remove packages. Validate package identity before deletion.\npnputil /enum-drivers\npnputil /delete-driver oemXX.inf /uninstall /force\nVerification checklist\nTarget device instance no longer references the removed package.\nNo stale network adapter entries remain for removed instances.\nReinstall path loads the intended package version.\nPost-reinstall link and IP behavior are validated.\nPartial uninstall recovery\nIf the package remains in the store, repeat package enumeration and removal with elevated permissions.\nIf stale adapters remain, remove hidden/non-present device instances and rescan hardware.\nIf automatic reinstall picks an unintended package, pin the intended package in your deployment flow before reconnecting."
